WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:04.304
-Our next guest has released
his latest comedy special,

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:06.272
"Out To Lunch,"
for free on YouTube.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.541
Please welcome
the very funny Mark Normand!

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:09.942
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:11.577
-Hey, hey.
Comedian Mark Normand here.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.611
We're in New York City,

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:14.314
great town for comedy,
but not anymore.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.183
The clubs are closed.
So we got to get creative.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:20.753
Let's try this
floating comedy club.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:24.557
[ Applause ]

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:25.892
Comedy!

00:00:25.892 --> 00:00:29.195
[ Foghorn blows ]

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.763
Hey, hey, folks!

00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:32.565
Here we are on
the Staten Island Ferry

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:33.899
in New York City.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.568
Whoo!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:35.568 --> 00:00:38.037
Thanks for coming out.
This is good times.

00:00:38.037 --> 00:00:39.205
Good to be here.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:40.339
This is kind of like
being on the Titanic,

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:43.042
except it's the economy
that's sinking.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:46.012
Yeah, yeah,
these are crazy times.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:47.113
I can't believe we're all here

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.881
'cause some guy
made love to a bat.

00:00:48.881 --> 00:00:52.952
Speaking of bats, they actually
shut down the production of

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:56.089
the movie "Batman"
because Batman got corona,

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:57.423
which doesn't shock me too much,

00:00:57.423 --> 00:01:00.927
'cause the wrong part
of his face is covered.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:03.596
Man, corona's starting to feel
like the "check engine" light.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.164
At first, it's scary,
but after a while, you're like,

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:06.165
"Screw it.

00:01:06.165 --> 00:01:08.467
I got to go to work."

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:09.936
This has been a wild year.

00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:13.373
2020. This is the only year my
therapist has ever recommended

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:16.742
I start living in the past.

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:19.579
I watch the news every day.
It's a big bummer.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:21.180
I think everybody knows that.

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.949
How about that Fauci?
He's cute.

00:01:22.949 --> 00:01:24.017
Oh, yeah.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:26.085
Fauci -- he's like
a COVID groundhog.

00:01:26.085 --> 00:01:27.286
Every time I see him, I'm like,

00:01:27.286 --> 00:01:29.755
"Aah, we got
six more weeks of pandemic."

00:01:29.755 --> 00:01:32.091
Oh, he's so little. I love him.

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:35.227
Yeah, the NBA.
That's weird, too.

00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:37.363
There's no one in the seats.
How eerie is that?

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.931
No one in the seats
at the NBA games.

00:01:38.931 --> 00:01:39.965
I got an idea.

00:01:39.965 --> 00:01:41.935
All those racist statues
you tore down?

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:44.103
Let's put them in the seats.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:46.172
I think that would
motivate the players.

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.440
You know, LeBron's
like, "Is that Robert E. Lee?

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.709
Alright,
we got to win this one."

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:53.413
Yeah, everybody needs
a break right now.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:56.182
I went to the hot-dog-eating
contest in Brooklyn.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.583
It was nice, but I got to say,

00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.752
the hot dog is the
perfect symbol for America,

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:02.455
because it's enjoyable, but once
you find out how it was made,

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:03.456
you're like, "Ooh!

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.658
I didn't want to know."

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.393
We all got to come together.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.761
A lot of tension out there.

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.329
I have no hatred
towards any group.

00:02:10.329 --> 00:02:12.197
You know, we're all
the same color on the inside.

00:02:12.197 --> 00:02:14.834
Well, except for smokers.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.502
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.070
Everybody's
upset about something.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:19.505
Everybody's
very sensitive right now.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:20.973
My buddy's a vegan. Ooh!

00:02:20.973 --> 00:02:22.875
I'm walking on eggshells
around this guy.

00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.711
He really hates that.

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:29.281
Yeah, I went to
a strip club in Texas.

00:02:29.281 --> 00:02:31.484
Man, it's so weird.
The women have to wear masks.

00:02:31.484 --> 00:02:32.719
It's crazy.

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:35.455
I had to go get
a private dance, you know,

00:02:35.455 --> 00:02:37.356
and the stripper was like,
"Hey, tell me a joke."

00:02:37.356 --> 00:02:38.858
I'm like,
"Look, I'm not at work.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.159
You are."

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:42.896
I brought my girlfriend to
a pet shop.

00:02:42.896 --> 00:02:44.330
You got to get a dog these days.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.398
That will make you feel better.

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:46.666
Brought my girlfriend
to a pet shop.

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:47.900
Geez Louise!

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.403
The pet shop -- that is
the strip club for women.

00:02:50.403 --> 00:02:52.338
A woman in a pet shop is like
a horny guy at a strip club.

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:53.506
She just walks in.

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.040
She can barely handle it like,
"Oh, my God.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.609
I want to touch them all."

00:02:56.609 --> 00:02:57.977
I had to be like, "Hey, relax.

00:02:57.977 --> 00:03:01.080
Some of these are broken homes.
They might bite you."

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.982
Yeah, she was just going down
the line like a horny guy.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.450
"That one's beautiful.
That one's gorgeous.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.719
That's my favorite.
I like that one the best."

00:03:06.719 --> 00:03:08.020
You know?

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.455
The manager was like,
"Hey, that's Roxy.

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:12.725
Everybody likes Roxy.
Yeah, yeah. Bring over Roxy."

00:03:12.725 --> 00:03:14.460
Yeah, now they go to
a private area.

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:16.095
They put her on her lap.
They're having a great time.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:17.797
She's like, "I swear to God,
Roxy's in love with me."

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.033
I'm like, "No, she's just
looking for a better life."

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:23.803
Thanks a lot. I'm Kevin Hart.
Enjoy the second wave.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:26.672
Thank you, New York!
Have a good night.

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:28.140
Comedy!

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:29.775
[ Sea gulls squawking ]

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.811
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:32.979
-Mark Normand.

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:36.082
For more info,
visit marknormandcomedy.com.

